  "live_records": {
    "q-36831": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36831",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=1.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
